Title: "Builds"
Id: "b8cfcb46-7573-4508-9e30-92f8a7c60664"

Text: "A build views an expression at a stated type with `\type@value`.

```mlg-fragment
\set@{x_ : x_ is \real}
\rational@k
```

A build succeeds when the value already has the target type, reaches it through
a `Declares:` extension, or has an applicable `Enables: view:`. It is checked;
`@` is not a way to force an unrelated value into a type.

```mlg-fragment
[\integer]
Declares: n
Enables:
. view:
  as: r := \as.rational{n} is \rational
```

A top-level build on the right of a `Defines:` assignment supplies its required
explicit type: `Defines: X := \set@{...}` is the typed alternative to an `is`
declaration plus separate body.

The former hard build `@!`, hard type introduction `is!`, and
`Enables: relation:`/`represents:` coercion syntax have been removed."
Id: "b76683ca-a9fb-48e3-9e79-5156e30e0a96"
